From 5c4401baab109f30086880dae201096337b87d5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:39:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] drv_helpers: Do not pad the pitch of NV12 and NV21 dumb
 buffers

The llvmpipe tile alignment rounds the pitch of every dumb buffer up to a
multiple of 64. Camera receivers without stride registers, such as the
SC7730 DCAM, write NV12 with the chroma plane right after width x height
bytes of luma, while the gralloc layout puts it at pitch x height. For a
2576x1932 still the pitch became 2624: the JPEG encoder read the chroma
plane 36 lines too late, colours were shifted and the last lines green.
Smaller sizes such as 800x480 (pitch 832) are affected the same way.

Keep the pitch of NV12 and NV21 buffers at their width. The height stays
aligned; it only adds space after the chroma plane.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Change-Id: Id43de15077c5d2202048df592a916279392f4b38
---
 drv_helpers.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drv_helpers.c b/drv_helpers.c
index 09f3096..73d2bc8 100644
--- a/drv_helpers.c
+++ b/drv_helpers.c
@@ -403,7 +403,16 @@ int drv_dumb_bo_create_ex(struct bo *bo, uint32_t width, uint32_t height, uint32
 		 * JPEG size, away from where the framework looks for it.
 		 */
 		if (aligned_height > 1) {
-			aligned_width = ALIGN(aligned_width, MESA_LLVMPIPE_TILE_SIZE);
+			/*
+			 * Camera receivers without stride registers (SC7730
+			 * DCAM) write NV12/NV21 with the chroma plane right
+			 * after width x height bytes of luma; a padded pitch
+			 * moves the chroma plane of the gralloc layout away
+			 * from it (2576 -> 2624 shifted the colours of 5 MP
+			 * stills by 36 lines).
+			 */
+			if (format != DRM_FORMAT_NV12 && format != DRM_FORMAT_NV21)
+				aligned_width = ALIGN(aligned_width, MESA_LLVMPIPE_TILE_SIZE);
 			aligned_height = ALIGN(aligned_height, MESA_LLVMPIPE_TILE_SIZE);
 		}
 		create_dumb.bpp = layout_from_format(format)->bytes_per_pixel[0] * 8;
